SUMMARY:The 9th Annual We the Future Social Justice Conference!
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 24\, 2026\, from 9:00am – 2:30pm\, Santa Rosa Junior College and North Bay Organizing Projects invites you to attend the 9th Annual We the Future Social Justice Conference!\nThis year’s conference centers the truth that joy and resistance are not opposites — they are intertwined liberatory practices. Joy fuels resistance. Resistance protects the conditions for joy. Together\, they form the heartbeat of collective liberation.\nWe the Future 2026 calls us to gather\, learn\, heal\, create\, and act together — rooting in joy\, practicing resistance\, and shaping liberatory futures in community. We are thrilled to welcome this year’s keynote speaker\, Prisca Dorcas Mojica Rodríguez\, who is a writer\, organizer\, and public intellectual whose work centers the lived experiences of undocumented and formerly undocumented Latine communities.\nCome and explore through three pathways: Educate. Activate. Create.\nSave your spot and register to attend this free event at wethefuture.santarosa.edu.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/the-9th-annual-we-the-future-social-justice-conference/
LOCATION:SRJC Petaluma Campus\, Sonoma Mountain Pkwy #680\, Petaluma\, 94954
CATEGORIES:Other
END:VEVENT
